    "summary": "Electrifying Fillmore East set with strong Pigpen numbers and tight Tighten Up jam",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a standout Pigpen acoustic set highlighted by \"Attics Of My Life\" and a fiery \"Turn On Your Lovelight.\" Jerry Garcia shines on acoustic guitar, steel guitar with the New Riders, and leads a tight \"Tighten Up\" jam. Overall pacing and transitions are praised as magical.",
    "review": "On July 12 1970 at the Fillmore East the Dead rolled out an unforgettable night that still feels fresh for listeners today. The first set unfurled a soulful Pigpen‑driven acoustic stretch – \"Attics Of My Life\" glowed, \"How Long Blues\" and \"It's A Man's World\" were delivered with raw feeling, and Garcia’s voice added a plaintive edge. After a brief New Riders interlude where Jerry swapped his six‑string for steel guitar, the electric band surged back in early morning hours, locking into a funky, tight \"Tighten Up\" jam that showcases the group’s chemistry. The second set kept the momentum with classics like \"Turn On Your Lovelight\" and a rollicking \"Dancin' In The Street,\" while the encore‑closing \"Uncle John's Band\" wrapped the night on a high note. Though audience recordings vary in clarity, the energy captured is unmistakable – a magical flow of acoustic intimacy into electric fire that makes this Fillmore East show a must‑hear snapshot of the early ’70 Dead.",
